                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      when i write code as follows:<br/>
{code}<br/>
PDDocument document = PDDocument.load(DOCUMENT_FILE);<br/>
DomXmpParser parser = new DomXmpParser();<br/>
XMPMetadata metadata = parser.parse(document.getDocumentCatalog().getMetadata().getStream().getUnfilteredStream());<br/>
metadata.removeSchema(metadata.getPDFIdentificationSchema());<br/>
File out = new File(OUTPUT_PATH);<br/>
OutputStream res = new FileOutputStream(out);<br/>
new XmpSerializer().serialize(metadata, res, true);<br/>
{code}<br/>
I get xml with following tags hierarchy:<br/>
{code}<br/>
&lt;rdf:Description xmlns:xmp=&quot;http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/&quot; CreateDate=&quot;2015-03-10T17:19:21+01:00&quot; CreatorTool=&quot;veraPDF Test Builder&quot; ModifyDate=&quot;2015-03-10T17:19:21+01:00&quot; rdf:about=&quot;&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xmp:CreateDate&gt;2015-03-10T17:19:21+01:00&lt;/xmp:CreateDate&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xmp:CreatorTool&gt;veraPDF Test Builder&lt;/xmp:CreatorTool&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xmp:ModifyDate&gt;2015-03-10T17:19:21+01:00&lt;/xmp:ModifyDate&gt;<br/>
&lt;/rdf:Description&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
It`s happens when some properties used in attributes. If this properties in source file used in tags then no problems.
