                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I am using PDFTextStripper and overriding processTextPosition so that I can test for white on white text.<br/>
<br/>
In version 1.8 I called getGraphicsState().getStrokingColor() and getGraphicsState().getNonStrokingColor() to get the colors and then could test for white on white text.<br/>
<br/>
In version 2.0 I am making the same calls on the same file, but the PDColor returned for both methods never changes from PDColor{components=[0.0], patternName=null}<br/>
<br/>
In the attached file, there is some white text &#39;661.37&#39; just above and to the left of the 2.00.  Can find it in Acrobat by searching or careful selecting
  </td>
