</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I came across a PDF document with missing type in the page dictionary. According to the spec that&#39;s required and PDFBox has a check and throws an IllegalState if the page is requested to the PDPageTree. Acrobat and other libs handle the same doc so I think the constraint could be relaxed a little, consider valid if type is Page or missing, and consider invalid if it&#39;s something else, what do you think?
  </td>
