    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 02/Dec/15 12:24 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 17/Mar/16 19:07 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 03/Dec/15 19:55 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Crypto,                     Parsing,                     PDModel            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      SecurityHandler fails to decrypt empty strings in a AES 128 encrypted PDF. <br/>
<br/>
Strings like: &lt;&lt;/Name ()&gt;&gt;<br/>
<br/>
This is because it tries to read the first 16 bytes as the AES IV, failing which it throws IOException. Solution: if you cannot read any bytes from the stream, it is empty and so there is nothing to decrypt.
