</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 7 Professional, 32 bit
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hi and thanks a lot for your great library!<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve noticed that after I merge two or more PDFs that the font of the merged PDF differs from that of the input PDFs.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve created a minimal project that lets you reproduce the bug:<br/>
https://github.com/mb720/PdfMerging<br/>
<br/>
When you start the program using &quot;./gradlew run&quot;, it will create three PDFs in &quot;~/Desktop/&quot;: Two simple PDFs with one page of text and a third one that is created by merging the first two PDFs.<br/>
<br/>
In the project the font I use is DroidSans.ttf. The version of PDFBox is 2.0.0-RC3.<br/>
<br/>
For reasons I don&#39;t know the problem does not occur on my Linux Mint Debian Edition 64 bit.<br/>
<br/>
Thanks a lot in advance,<br/>
Matthias
  </td>
