                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        PDFBOX-2384                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      OS X 10.11.4, Java 1.8.0_73-b02
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When running the command line {{ExtractText}} with the {{-html}} flag, the output file always has the following meta tag specifying UTF-16 regardless of the actual output encoding:<br/>
<br/>
{code:html}<br/>
&lt;meta http-equiv=&quot;Content-Type&quot; content=&quot;text/html; charset=&quot;UTF-16&quot;&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
This causes editors that respect the meta tag (emacs, etc.) to garble the file content.
  </td>
