                                            <td class="assignee">            Andreas Lehmkühler
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Cyril Bremaud
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Cyril Bremaud
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/Apr/16 08:19 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Apr/16 11:45 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 11/Apr/16 11:45 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Crypto,                     Parsing            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        PDFBOX-2963                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I would like to be able to use my own provider to sign encrypted files. Indeed, org.apache.pdfbox.pdmodel.encryption.SecurityHandlerFactory forces the use of org.bouncycastle.jce.provider.BouncyCastleProvider.<br/>
<br/>
A solution is to make SecurityHandlerFactory uses a java.security.Provider instead.<br/>
Thank you.<br/>
<br/>

