                <tr id="issuerow12973905" rel="12973905" data-issuekey="PDFBOX-3368" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    PDFBox
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="PDFBOX-3368" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PDFBOX-3368">PDFBOX-3368</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                ContainsKey don&#39;t work for the Map&lt;String, Object&gt; returned by PDStructureTreeRoot.getRoleMap
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Trivial
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Andreas Lehmkühler
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Carlos Cabral
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Carlos Cabral
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 30/May/16 07:30 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Mar/17 18:13 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 30/May/16 16:20 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.8.12,                     2.0.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.8.13,                     2.0.2,                     3.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        PDModel            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate">86400</td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate">86400</td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">            0%
    </td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 10
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      No sure if it is an expected behaviour or a bug.<br/>
<br/>
The Method PDStructureTreeRoot.getRoleMap returns a map which the key is a String (Map&lt;String, Object&gt;).<br/>
<br/>
However when we use map.containsKey(&quot;Header&quot;) it always return false because instead of a String it is waiting for A COSName instance.<br/>
Then we have to use  map.containsKey(COSName.getPDFName(&quot;Header&quot;));<br/>
<br/>
In the other the method map.get(&quot;Header&quot;); works<br/>
<br/>
{code:title=Test.java}<br/>
//PDF Filte tested: <br/>
//http://www.adobe.com/content/dam/Adobe/en/devnet/acrobat/pdfs/PDF32000_2008.pdf<br/>
try (PDDocument document = PDDocument.load(new File(&quot;PDF32000_2008.pdf&quot;));){<br/>
  PDStructureTreeRoot treeRoot = document.getDocumentCatalog().getStructureTreeRoot();<br/>
  Map&lt;String, Object&gt; roleMap = treeRoot.getRoleMap();<br/>
  //Returned map: COSDictionaryMap&lt;K,V&gt;<br/>
  System.out.println(roleMap.containsKey(&quot;Header&quot;));//No work<br/>
  System.out.println(  roleMap.containsKey(COSName.getPDFName(&quot;Header&quot;)));//Works<br/>
} catch (IOException ex) {  <br/>
  ex.printStackTrace();<br/>
}<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
