                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 7, jre 1.8 , 
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Here&#39;s a segment of my code.<br/>
//code<br/>
try<br/>
{<br/>
PDFRenderer pdfRenderer = new PDFRenderer(pdDoc);<br/>
 BufferedImage image = pdfRenderer.renderImageWithDPI(page-1, 300,ImageType.GRAY);<br/>
 ImageIOUtil.writeImage(image,&quot;G:/Trial/tempImg.png&quot;, 300);<br/>
//some codes 1<br/>
}<br/>
catch(Exception e)<br/>
{<br/>
//printing something<br/>
}<br/>
finally{<br/>
//some codes 2<br/>
}<br/>
//code<br/>
When I debugged this code, i saw that just after the line renderImage withDPI ,control reaches finally and just after finally I get out of memory error. After the buffered image line ideally control sgould execute &quot;some codes 1&quot; which are just after that line but instead control skips all that and reaches finally, it doesnt even go to catch , so I cant understand why is this happening.<br/>
Please provide some insight on this.
