                <tr id="issuerow13005201" rel="13005201" data-issuekey="PDFBOX-3498" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    PDFBox
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="PDFBOX-3498" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PDFBOX-3498">PDFBOX-3498</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Unexpected spaces in text extraction
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Tilman Hausherr
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Tilman Hausherr
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Tilman Hausherr
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 15/Sep/16 16:06 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Mar/17 18:13 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 15/Sep/16 16:26 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.2,                     2.0.3            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.4,                     3.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Text extraction            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In the tests by [~tallison@apache.org] regressions were found with files from Delaware courts, see reduced file attached.<br/>
<br/>
The extracted text with 2.0.2 and 2.0.3 is<br/>
{code}<br/>
IN THE  COUR T OF  CHAN CER Y O F TH E STA TE OF  D ELA WARE<br/>
{code}<br/>
in 2.0.1 and 1.8 it was<br/>
{code}<br/>
IN THE COURT OF CHANCERY OF THE STATE OF DELAWARE<br/>
{code}<br/>
The cause is the /W ranges table:<br/>
{code}<br/>
/W [1 1 0 2 3 250 4 10 0 11<br/>
12 333 13 14 0 15 15 250 16 16<br/>
333 17 17 250 18 18 277 19 19 0<br/>
20 23 500 24 35 0 36 36 722 37<br/>
37 666 38 39 722 40 40 666 41 41<br/>
610 42 43 777 44 44 389 45 45 0<br/>
46 46 777 47 47 666 48 48 943 49<br/>
49 722 50 50 777 51 51 610 52 52<br/>
0 53 53 722 54 54 556 55 55 666<br/>
56 57 722 59 59 0 60 60 722 61<br/>
67 0 68 68 500 69 69 556 70 70<br/>
443 71 71 556 72 72 443 73 73 333<br/>
74 74 500 75 75 556 76 76 277 77<br/>
77 0 78 78 556 79 79 277 80 80<br/>
833 81 81 556 82 82 500 83 84 556<br/>
85 85 443 86 86 389 87 87 333 88<br/>
88 556 89 89 0 90 90 722 91 92<br/>
500 93 178 0 179 180 500 181 181 0<br/>
182 182 333 183 751 0 752 752 198 753<br/>
794 0 795 795 612 796 1126 0 1127 1127<br/>
125 1129 1129 2000 1130 65534 0]<br/>
{code}<br/>
For text extraction, the width of a space is caculated by taking an average of all widths. However these files have a lot (over 60000) of widths that are 0. So I&#39;ll just ignore widths &lt;= 0, as it is already done in PDFont.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
