                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      {code}<br/>
Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; java.lang.ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException: 1<br/>
        at java.awt.color.ICC_ColorSpace.fromRGB(Unknown Source)<br/>
        at org.apache.pdfbox.pdmodel.graphics.color.PDICCBased.loadICCProfile(PDICCBased.java:145)<br/>
        at org.apache.pdfbox.pdmodel.graphics.color.PDICCBased.&lt;init&gt;(PDICCBased.java:89)<br/>
{code}<br/>
The line that triggers this is this new line<br/>
{code}<br/>
awtColorSpace.fromRGB(new float[3]);<br/>
{code}<br/>
According to the javadoc ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException happens only if the input array is smaller than 3.... I&#39;ll just add ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException to the catch list. Probably yet another JDK bug.
  </td>
