                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      PDType1Font.java has a predefined list of fonts like Times-Roman, Helvetica, Courier, Symbol and ZapfDingbats.<br/>
<br/>
When creating a pdf/A, the font is embedded and not taken from the reader&#39;s operating system.<br/>
As per https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helvetica_(Schriftart) , this may lead to a licensing issue.<br/>
<br/>
Suggestions:<br/>
1) Use a free font such as <br/>
https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nimbus_Sans_L instead<br/>
2) at least warn in JavaDoc about the issue<br/>
<br/>
Or is it an non-issue?
  </td>
