</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Consider the following abstract form tree:<br/>
* Field F<br/>
** /FT /Tx<br/>
** /DA /Helv 9 Tf 0 g<br/>
** Kids<br/>
*** Annot Kid1<br/>
**** /DA /Helv 12 Tf 0 g<br/>
*** Annot Kid2<br/>
<br/>
If you execute F.setValue(&quot;XY&quot;), the default appearance font size of F is applied on all Annotations effectively overriding the font size of Kid1, which should be 12 after all.<br/>
The same happens when you execute a form.flatten(field[], true), because the appearance characteristics are refreshed, but again only considering the field&#39;s DA and not the annotations&#39; DA font size.
  </td>
