</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        PDFBOX-3789                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 10
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I tried to convert a PDF file to an image. But there is a error with the character width computation. As you can see inside the blue box, there are gaps after every umlaut mark (ä ,ö ,ü). Some characters in the font doesn&#39;t contain any width information. The distance between the character is handled by position adjustment. For example:<br/>
<br/>
[1., -278, ), -844, H, -722, ä, -556, u, -611, sliche P, -667, f, -333, lege] TJ<br/>
<br/>
I guess there is an error in the font.getWidth() implementation. If I call font.getWidth(&quot;ä&quot;) it returns 556. (Instead of 0, what would fit)<br/>
<br/>
I attached the PDF and the converted image.<br/>

  </td>
