</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Mac, JDK8
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hi,<br/>
<br/>
I tried using the Signature example (https://svn.apache.org/viewvc/pdfbox/trunk/examples/src/main/java/org/apache/pdfbox/examples/signature/) which works great for certifying pdfs. <br/>
<br/>
However if I want to certify and replace the original pdf without creating a new one (like foo_signed.pdf should only be foo.pdf), I get an exception:<br/>
<br/>
`Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; java.io.IOException: Error: End-of-File, expected line pdfbox`<br/>
<br/>
I invoked the method like this (L215 of CreateSignature.java): <br/>
`signing.signDetached(inFile);`<br/>
<br/>
How would I change the example so that I can certify pdfs without creating copy files?<br/>

  </td>
